[
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Model",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"max-single-feature-share\", \"Threshold\": 0.6}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "single-feature-dominance",
      "Rationale": "Every model kind — glass-box or trained — is invalid if one feature already contains the answer; dominance is leakage until a human signs off."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "0B008475-D78B-52DC-A171-E92B9DE5317A"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Model",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"min-rows-per-feature\", \"Threshold\": 5}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "min-rows-per-feature",
      "Rationale": "No model family below can learn anything real with fewer than a handful of rows per feature."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "FDDAA79B-7040-52C4-99C8-643892D4BFAF"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Model",
      "PropertyKey": "ValidationDefaults",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Strategy\": \"train_test_split\", \"TestSize\": 0.2, \"LockedHoldoutFraction\": 0.1}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Honest-holdout discipline applies to every trainable descendant; given-mode rubrics simply report holdout metrics without searching."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "9E65BD51-114F-592E-92F0-1257527E2827"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Linear",
      "PropertyKey": "CompatibleProblemTypes",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "[\"classification\", \"regression\"]",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Every linear member handles both shapes (logistic for classification, ridge/rubric for either)."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "580C7C4F-690E-57BF-840F-4272552A5D13"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Linear",
      "PropertyKey": "Explainability",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "per-record-exact",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Coefficients give exact signed per-record contributions for every linear member — this is the family’s defining property."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "DE021FAD-94D3-59A0-8CFD-F61AF58AA29B"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Linear",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"impute\", \"strategy\": \"median\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "impute",
      "Rationale": "Linear members cannot tolerate missing values; imputation is always in their kit."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "8FB42695-F75A-5B72-8455-BCF97F9079E7"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Linear",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"standardize\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "standardize",
      "Rationale": "Comparable coefficient magnitudes — and regularization fairness — require standardized inputs for every linear member."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "A3A2AE4C-61FE-593F-9DDC-0C3DF3A96ED8"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Linear",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"C/alpha\", \"kind\": \"l2-strength\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "regularization",
      "Rationale": "All linear members expose one regularization-strength knob."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "01A40F54-2624-589C-99D8-D3F1DB58A0EA"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Tree Ensemble",
      "PropertyKey": "CompatibleProblemTypes",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "[\"classification\", \"regression\"]",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Every tree-ensemble member supports both problem shapes."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "AB51FDCC-28C0-587E-B5EF-A2C8CCF17F11"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Tree Ensemble",
      "PropertyKey": "Explainability",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "global-importance",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Trees give global feature importance but not exact per-record attributions (those need SHAP, which no member ships yet)."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "5A0E00C6-E0E9-520F-A9D8-7BBC5422862A"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Tree Ensemble",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"impute\", \"strategy\": \"median\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "impute",
      "Rationale": "Tree members handle scale natively but not NaN in this sidecar; imputation is the one transform they all need."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "43E8B379-088F-57FC-B3B4-FA83519F2323"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Tree Ensemble",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"n_estimators\", \"range\": [50, 1000]}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "n_estimators",
      "Rationale": "Every ensemble has a tree count."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "9421C701-5627-53EC-986E-1C3B3EEFF63F"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Tree Ensemble",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"max_depth\", \"range\": [2, 16]}",
      "Sequence": 1,
      "ItemKey": "max_depth",
      "Rationale": "Every ensemble bounds tree depth."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "26EE4874-B954-5C65-AA64-7FC1C00E9753"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Boosting",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"learning_rate\", \"range\": [0.005, 0.3]}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "learning_rate",
      "Rationale": "Sequential correction is paced by a learning rate in every boosting member; bagging members have none."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "6BB36990-3E2F-51D1-9CDB-A121C61B903C"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Boosting",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"subsample\", \"range\": [0.5, 1.0]}",
      "Sequence": 1,
      "ItemKey": "subsample",
      "Rationale": "Stochastic boosting rate — common to XGBoost and LightGBM."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "C9135212-D2AB-5793-8354-9CBD6E0B5EB7"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "CompatibleProblemTypes",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "[\"classification\", \"regression\"]",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "The MLP member supports both problem shapes."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "1384DB76-FFE0-50AE-A55F-490FA21525C2"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "Explainability",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "none",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "No neural member offers faithful per-feature attribution today; claiming otherwise would be dishonest."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "76D9D02F-AB8B-5BFF-A6EA-4E332B591A4A"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"impute\", \"strategy\": \"mean\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "impute",
      "Rationale": "Dense nets require complete inputs."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "DF8BD169-3DAD-5787-B732-E21F9776989D"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"standardize\", \"required\": true}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "standardize",
      "Rationale": "Unscaled inputs break gradient training for every neural member — this is required, not advisory."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "B78FF3C4-5402-5B68-8730-1104E199D733"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Replace",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"min-rows-per-feature\", \"Threshold\": 50}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "min-rows-per-feature",
      "Rationale": "Neural members need far more data per feature than the Model-root floor."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "14BB9EA0-E871-53F1-81F9-6FBAA741D64C"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Sequence",
      "PropertyKey": "CompatibleProblemTypes",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "[\"sequence\"]",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Sequence members consume ordered per-entity events — a different problem type, not a variant of classification."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "351C794F-498D-5654-B0C6-263F1ABDAAD3"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Sequence",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"requires-ordered-sequences\", \"MinLength\": 3}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "requires-ordered-sequences",
      "Rationale": "Without ordered per-entity sequences of some minimum length, no sequence member is meaningful."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "9A6C0402-608F-53C7-9CB4-55EA73D863D4"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Structure",
      "PropertyKey": "Explainability",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "inherits-min-of-fillers",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "A wrapper can never be more explainable than the least explainable component filling its slots."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "900FCE0D-40C2-562C-A5DA-D3BB34423434"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Structure",
      "PropertyKey": "CompatibleProblemTypes",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "[\"classification\", \"regression\"]",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Shipped wrappers compose tabular models; sequence wrapping is out of scope."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "CCCB2811-900C-5527-BE75-BCA99E16A748"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Scaling",
      "PropertyKey": "GuidanceRationale",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "Population-relative: parameters are fit ONCE on the training population and frozen onto the model, never re-fit at scoring — the anti-skew guarantee.",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "fit-once",
      "Rationale": "True of every scaling member by construction."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "3A60F64E-DD09-5930-8D7E-9E414FEAB23B"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Curve Mapping",
      "PropertyKey": "GuidanceRationale",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "Stateless and parameterized: the operator sets the curve; nothing is fit. Identical at train and score by definition.",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "stateless",
      "Rationale": "Definitional for the family."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "CF66C5E1-DB68-5BD5-86FC-2C0A26BEEFFC"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Input",
      "PropertyKey": "MissingDataPolicy",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "Zero",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "Rationale": "Absent evidence defaults to contributing nothing — the conservative floor every input starts from; models and rubrics may override per binding."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "218BB21A-856C-58D8-AFCB-F10C818520CF"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=As-Of Aggregate",
      "PropertyKey": "GuidanceRationale",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "Only rows dated at or before the as-of instant may enter the window; using AsOfStrategy Mode=none with these inputs builds a model that has seen the future.",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "leakage-boundary",
      "Rationale": "The defining constraint of every as-of member."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "73E01AF8-4BC3-5543-8EB4-0A8C82BEF996"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Code Feature",
      "PropertyKey": "GuidanceRationale",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "An Action-backed input must have PromotionState=Approved before it can feed a trained or served model; Draft/InReview code never moves persisted predictions.",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "promotion-gate",
      "Rationale": "The gate is the family contract, ported from Sonar."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "FA18B77E-D8A5-5F3F-AA0A-47A8ED1B1FE4"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Model",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"class-balance\", \"MinMinorityFraction\": 0.02}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "class-balance",
      "Rationale": "True of every model family: a minority class below a couple of percent makes accuracy meaningless and any family judged on it look excellent while being useless. Evaluates only when the problem is classification; a regression candidate reports Unevaluated rather than a false pass."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "08367A53-211A-425B-99C0-F199D0625E8E"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.430Z",
      "checksum": "d201f6950822f4ff69b3303b61cb6405f759ab2da006823dcf4046e8ddac2c8e"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Tree Ensemble",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"high-cardinality\", \"MaxDistinct\": 100}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "max-cardinality",
      "Rationale": "Every tree member splits on categories one at a time, so a very high-cardinality column produces splits that memorize rather than generalize. Linear and neural members one-hot instead, which fails differently, so this belongs here and not on Model."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "A0783675-C8E2-4F53-BB4B-97BD28BD08C5"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.448Z",
      "checksum": "28422ded0504aa9d47b4cf32f77521443db179ae57c0e93d2c9ceee21b6090d0"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "StatisticalGate",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"Kind\": \"requires-direction-per-input\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "requires-direction-per-input",
      "Rationale": "A rubric combines normalized inputs by hand-set weights, so every input must declare which direction is better. Without that the weighted sum is arithmetic with no meaning — and unlike a fitted family, nothing downstream will discover the direction for it."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "C344E627-1456-4987-BB85-0E3CFE8F7AAD"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.527Z",
      "checksum": "554196e15258c6fb4bb44984fc56739004ef6c2ab7102caf2f959b9fe5b36bff"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"minmax\", \"population_relative\": true}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "minmax",
      "Rationale": "A rubric's weights are only comparable across inputs that share a scale, and min-max is the population-relative normalization that produces one."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "EAD3BFD1-EB76-4611-8374-9F4737ED8E35"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.542Z",
      "checksum": "7caa30836a12b729de552e0a8ecbf8835beb68de6a326e3260ac557cd48339eb"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"percentile\", \"population_relative\": true}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "percentile",
      "Rationale": "Percentile ranking is the normalization to reach for when an input is skewed enough that min-max would let one outlier dominate the whole score."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "2A0B33ED-CD62-4CE1-82A5-35945333C2F1"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.554Z",
      "checksum": "ac5e5ed415bdb4fd743c7a8944cf7d9ae0b420db781e3b4394b6eab13ae96679"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"op\": \"zscore\", \"population_relative\": true, \"clamped\": true}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "zscore",
      "Rationale": "Clamped z-scoring keeps a roughly normal input on the same 0-1 footing as the others without letting a tail run away with the weight."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "C2CAB89C-A64B-435A-9CFB-717CA421BEE7"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.565Z",
      "checksum": "8eeea10b39e7338b75a65a21e4051aee64ba2beff8fafed252970be35253cbdc"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"weight_mode\", \"kind\": \"enum\", \"values\": [\"given\", \"search\"]}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "weight_mode",
      "Rationale": "The rubric is the one family that is first-class whether or not it is trained: `given` takes an operator's weights as authored, `search` fits non-negative weights. Both are legitimate models."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "7FD01D15-D530-4719-A55F-C4084465E956"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.580Z",
      "checksum": "f661077e11ce6ad41a374efafbd61ce96b2597506c4aeb8ee02eefbfc5b31b67"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"scale_min/scale_max\", \"kind\": \"range\", \"default\": [0, 100]}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "output_range",
      "Rationale": "A rubric's output is a score a human reads, so the range it lands in is a real choice rather than an implementation detail."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "E0852930-A2D4-42A0-A976-ED21F7EA3C61"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.594Z",
      "checksum": "b2aa096c7b6cd8a283bf3237f4e3e8844ecb680ffb4d5535c25d4e40b8c87b01"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Glass-Box Rubric",
      "PropertyKey": "MissingDataPolicy",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "\"Zero\"",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": null,
      "Rationale": "A rubric has to decide what a missing input contributes, and the choice is visible in the score: Zero scores it as absent, where NeutralMidpoint would score it as unknown and Exclude would renormalize the remaining weights. Fitted families let the imputer make this decision quietly; a glass-box rubric must state it."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "45172EBA-8D8B-4517-9718-AC1B911B8C1A"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.606Z",
      "checksum": "cb356fa569b9915958e261b6121046a17cda207cfda39eef5e74f4ee5a4a7051"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"hidden_layer_sizes\", \"kind\": \"architecture\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "hidden_layer_sizes",
      "Rationale": "Every neural member has a hidden-layer shape, and it is the parameter that most changes what the model can represent."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "96CF02F8-36D2-4DA7-9E6E-11BDFFF5F904"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.480Z",
      "checksum": "be8eb9f589a47a4ecd14d1174abf002a2bc31f6be638372ed0445bcff8a7ffbf"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "HyperparameterBank",
      "Operation": "Add",
      "Value": "{\"name\": \"alpha\", \"kind\": \"l2-strength\"}",
      "Sequence": 0,
      "ItemKey": "alpha",
      "Rationale": "Neural members overfit small tabular data readily, so weight decay is the knob a search must be able to turn."
    },
    "primaryKey": {
      "ID": "3F07797F-EFC9-4141-B910-6A3779A2174E"
    },
    "sync": {
      "lastModified": "2026-09-04T03:37:32.491Z",
      "checksum": "8fae7491f49f8791214a038d2a55721c6df91b736f6de75cdcc814b9632883b1"
    }
  },
  {
    "fields": {
      "ComponentTypeID": "@lookup:MJ: ML Component Types.Name=Neural",
      "PropertyKey": "PreprocessingBank",
